<title>AUSTRALIA: Top 20 Australian Dividend Yields - April 28.</title>
<headline>Top 20 Australian Dividend Yields - April 28.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty highest dividend yields for Australian companies included in the 320-share All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday.</p>
<p>Dividends based on rolling 12 months.</p>
<p>Yields are not grossed up for franking credits.</p>
<p>					   Dividend</p>
<p>Rank Name		     Yield    Close</p>
<p> 1   Centro Prop	    16.09    2.16</p>
<p> 2   Mt Leyshon Gold	13.16    1.90</p>
<p> 3   Prime Credit Tr	 9.90    0.99</p>
<p> 4   Aust Tour		 9.74    0.77</p>
<p> 5   Prop Income Inv	 9.17    1.10</p>
<p> 6   BT Prop Trust	   9.12    1.79</p>
<p> 7   Villa World	     8.77    1.14</p>
<p> 8   Hills Inds		8.77    1.95</p>
<p> 9   Natl Consol	     8.65    1.04</p>
<p>10   Indu Property	   8.58    0.99</p>
<p>11   Gandel Retail Tr	8.58    0.91</p>
<p>12   Equitilink		8.47    0.59</p>
<p>13   Natl In Prop	    8.43    1.04</p>
<p>14   Countrywide-PP	  8.40    1.21</p>
<p>15   Gen Prop Tr	     8.27    2.43</p>
<p>16   Ipoh			8.26    2.18</p>
<p>17   Westfield Trust	 8.24    2.38</p>
